Phase 3 — Owner Application Integration Contract
1. Confirmed system facts
The current deployed Mainnet testnet-auth-issuer v4:
Validates the Pi access token through https://api.minepi.com/v2/me.
Signs the ordinary Testnet login assertion with ALBUKHR_TESTNET_GATEWAY_SECRET.
Does not create a Supabase client, read Mainnet public.users, inspect public.projects, or prove project ownership.
Issues a general login assertion, not a project-specific Owner assertion.
The Testnet testnet-auth-gateway v5:
Verifies that ordinary login assertion against fixed issuer/audience/network rules.
Consumes one-use nonces and issues a short-lived Testnet access code/session.
Is a login/session gateway and must not be repurposed as the Owner application proof endpoint.
The current Testnet registry sync:
Reads Mainnet get_public_project_registry('mainnet').
Its validator preserves each registry project's id in the normalized payload.
get_public_project_registry returns the Mainnet project UUID (id) but does not return owner_albukhr_user_id or Owner identity.
apply_mainnet_approved_project_mirror(jsonb) ignores the incoming id and mirrors/upserts by project_code; it stores only Testnet-local project data and registration_source='mainnet-approved-mirror'.
Therefore registration_source alone is not sufficient proof of which Mainnet row a Testnet project mirrors.
The existing Testnet Owner API v8:
Uses X-Testnet-Session, hashes it with SHA-256, and checks testnet_sessions.
Resolves the Testnet public.users row using pi_uid and network='testnet'.
Reads Owner projects through projects.owner_user_id.
Must remain unchanged.
The current Testnet Owner Admin API v3:
Uses a separate bearer admin session stored in testnet_admin_sessions.
Checks network='testnet', expiry, revocation, and roles containing super_admin.
Enforces scoped_projects.
Calls the legacy Owner-management RPC. The new application Admin route must be separate and must not call that RPC.
The Testnet project detail page:
Loads js/testnet-project.js, js/testnet-gateway-auth.js, js/testnet-api-core.js, and the legacy Owner visibility bridge.
js/testnet-project.js exposes window.AlbukhrTestnetProject.getProject() and emits albukhr:testnet-project-loaded / albukhr:testnet-project-rendered.
project.html already loads the Pi SDK.
Testnet login obtains a Pi access token, sends it to the direct-auth endpoint, then clears it. It is not retained by the project page.
window.AlbukhrTestnetAuth.getSessionToken() provides the current Testnet session to new frontend modules. Continue using the existing short-lived Testnet session; do not store Pi access tokens.
2. Canonical Mainnet owner proof — separate issuer
Create a new Mainnet Edge Function:
testnet-project-owner-proof-issuer
Do not modify testnet-auth-issuer v4 or its login contract.
issue request
HTTP POST.
Authorization: Bearer <Pi access token> obtained from a fresh Pi SDK authentication initiated only after the user clicks the Owner application action.
JSON body: { "action": "issue", "project_code": "<current project code>" }.
CORS allows only the Testnet application origin https://test.albukhr.com for this browser use. The old login issuer's CORS behavior remains untouched.
Pi access token is memory-only; never write it to LocalStorage, SessionStorage, a URL, logs, or Testnet database.
Mainnet server-side checks
Call Pi /v2/me with the supplied Pi access token.
Require a non-empty verified uid.
Use Mainnet SUPABASE_URL plus SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY only in the Edge Function.
Resolve exactly one public.users row where pi_uid=<verified uid> and network='mainnet'.
Resolve exactly one Mainnet public.projects row where:
project_code=<requested code>;
network='mainnet';
project_type IN ('internal','external');
status IN ('approved','active');
owner_albukhr_user_id=<resolved Mainnet users.id>.
Do not accept the project UUID, user UUID, owner_albukhr_user_id, or project type supplied by the browser as authority. They are resolved server-side.
Signed proof claims
Use a dedicated, independent secret named ALBUKHR_TESTNET_OWNER_PROOF_SECRET, configured on both Mainnet issuer and Testnet verifier. Do not reuse ALBUKHR_TESTNET_GATEWAY_SECRET or the Admin gateway secret.
Claims:
Claim
Value / rule
iss
albukhr-mainnet
aud
albukhr-testnet-project-owner-proof
purpose
project_owner_application
source_network
mainnet
network
testnet
source_project_id
Exact Mainnet projects.id
project_code
Exact Mainnet project code
project_type
Verified internal or external
owner_pi_uid_hash
SHA-256 of verified Pi UID; never the raw UID
proof_id
Cryptographically random unique nonce/reference
