Unix seconds; lifetime at most 120 seconds
Never include Mainnet users.id or owner_albukhr_user_id in the signed claims or response.
3. Testnet proof verification and one-time ticket
Create a separate Testnet Edge Function:
testnet-project-owner-application
It authenticates the current applicant using X-Testnet-Session, following the existing testnet-project-owner v8 session pattern.
Proof verification action
Request fields:
action: "verify_owner_proof"
project_id: Testnet local project UUID
proof: signed Mainnet assertion
Server-side checks:
Validate Testnet session hash, expiry, revocation and network='testnet'.
Resolve public.users using the session Pi UID plus network='testnet'.
Verify the HMAC signature using ALBUKHR_TESTNET_OWNER_PROOF_SECRET with constant-time comparison.
Require exact iss, aud, purpose, source_network, network, iat, exp, and a non-empty proof ID.
Hash the current Testnet session pi_uid and compare it with owner_pi_uid_hash.
Resolve the Testnet project by id and network='testnet'.
Require project_type IN ('internal','external'), status IN ('approved','active'), and exact equality of project code/type with the proof.
Verify the Testnet project's private mirror provenance maps it to the exact source_project_id in the proof.
Reject if the Testnet project has a different non-null owner_user_id.
Consume proof_id once. Replay must fail.
On success, create a random opaque short-lived application ticket bound server-side to:
Testnet applicant user ID;
Testnet project ID;
Mainnet source project UUID;
proof ID hash;
expiry;
consumed state.
Return only the opaque ticket ID and safe project/application state. Do not return signed proof claims or Mainnet identity values.
Why a ticket is required
The Mainnet proof expires within 120 seconds. A one-time Testnet ticket allows the browser to submit the application form without retaining a reusable Mainnet proof. The ticket must be consumed atomically with the application insert.
4. Provenance repair — preserve the public registry contract
Do not add Mainnet Owner identifiers to get_public_project_registry.
The public Mainnet registry already returns projects.id, which is the source project UUID. Keep it as a project locator; it is not the Owner identity.
Add a private Testnet provenance table, conceptually:
private.mainnet_project_mirror_provenance
Fields:
testnet_project_id uuid primary key references public.projects(id);
mainnet_source_project_id uuid not null unique;
project_code text not null;
project_type text not null check (project_type IN ('internal','external','core'));
source_status text not null;
source_updated_at timestamptz;
last_verified_at timestamptz not null;
sync_batch_id uuid not null;
created_at, updated_at.
The mirror transaction must:
validate the incoming source id as a UUID;
verify project code/type/source state;
perform the existing Testnet project upsert by code;
resolve the resulting Testnet project UUID;
upsert the private provenance row mapping local Testnet project ID to exact Mainnet source project ID;
reject if a project code is already mapped to a different Mainnet source UUID, or a source UUID is already mapped to a different Testnet project;
update source status and verification timestamp in the same transaction;
mark provenance suspended/stale when the source project is removed or suspended.
Implement this additively in a forward-only migration and the existing registry sync call path, after source comparison. Do not change the current public registry payload by adding Owner identity fields. Do not allow browser roles to read provenance.
5. Application data model
Recommended application tables remain Testnet-only and separate from legacy Owner data:
public.testnet_project_owner_applications
id uuid primary key;
project_id uuid not null references public.projects(id);
network text not null check (network='testnet');
applicant_testnet_user_id uuid not null references public.users(id);
mainnet_source_project_id uuid not null (source project UUID is not an Owner UUID);
mainnet_source_project_code text not null;
mainnet_source_project_type text not null check (mainnet_source_project_type IN ('internal','external'));
owner_proof_ticket_id uuid not null;
status text not null check (status IN ('submitted','changes_requested','resubmitted','approved','rejected','withdrawn'));
owner_submission jsonb not null;
submitted_at, reviewed_at, created_at, updated_at;
reviewed_by uuid null references public.users(id);
review_note text null;
approved_testnet_user_id uuid null references public.users(id).
Partial unique index: one open application per project for statuses submitted, changes_requested, and resubmitted.
public.testnet_project_owner_application_history
Append-only transition log:
id uuid primary key;
application_id uuid not null references ...;
project_id uuid not null references public.projects(id);
network text not null check (network='testnet');
actor_testnet_user_id uuid null references public.users(id);
actor_role text not null check (actor_role IN ('owner','admin','system'));
action text not null check (action IN ('submitted','changes_requested','resubmitted','approved','rejected','withdrawn'));
from_status, to_status, note, metadata jsonb, created_at.
Proof ticket storage
Keep ticket/proof replay records in a service-only table or private table, not a public registry view. Store hashes of proof ID / ticket, not signed claims or raw Pi UID. Enforce unique proof ID and one-time ticket consumption atomically.
Table grants and RLS
Enable RLS on every new public-schema table.
Revoke direct SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE from anon and authenticated.
Grant only the narrow service role permissions needed by the Edge Functions/RPCs.
Public project registry functions must never join or return applications, proof tickets, provenance or applicant details.
No browser supplied user IDs, review status, admin identity or Mainnet Owner IDs are trusted.
6. Resubmission and Admin review
Owner routes
testnet-project-owner-application actions:
eligibility
verify_owner_proof
submit
resubmit
my_applications
Every route requires a valid X-Testnet-Session. The applicant user ID is resolved server-side.
submit accepts only applicant-entered business/team/contact/profile fields plus the opaque ticket. It must ignore or reject browser-supplied applicant_user_id, owner_user_id, mainnet_user_id, status, approval fields and reviewer fields.
resubmit is allowed only for the same applicant's application in changes_requested; it creates history and preserves prior content in the audit trail.
Separate Admin route
Create:
testnet-project-owner-application-admin
Do not modify testnet-project-owner-admin v3.
Admin authentication must follow the existing pattern:
Authorization: Bearer <Testnet admin session>;
hash token and resolve testnet_admin_sessions;
require network='testnet', not expired, not revoked;
require roles containing super_admin unless a separate authorized role is explicitly approved;
enforce scoped_projects for list and review actions.
Actions:
list_applications
review_application
The Admin sees Owner-submitted information read-only. Review decisions are changes_requested, approved, or rejected, each with a reason. Admin cannot type or override Owner identity values.
7. Mandatory Mainnet revalidation at approval
A Mainnet Owner proof that was valid at application time may no longer be valid when an Admin reviews the request.
Therefore, before Testnet approval:
Testnet Admin endpoint rechecks current Mainnet ownership through a new server-to-server verification action on the Mainnet proof issuer.
The internal request is authenticated with the dedicated ALBUKHR_TESTNET_OWNER_PROOF_SECRET, a short timestamp window and a request nonce.
Mainnet re-reads the exact source project, canonical Owner link, project type, status and the source Owner's Pi UID hash.
Mainnet confirms that the same Pi UID hash remains the canonical owner of that exact source project.
Testnet then calls its local approval RPC immediately, passing only a signed/opaque, short-lived revalidation result tied to application ID, Testnet project ID, source project ID and applicant user ID.
The local approval RPC must use row locks and atomically:
re-check Testnet network, project_type IN ('internal','external'), approved/active status and exact private provenance;
reject Core at SQL level, irrespective of UI or Edge Function behavior;
reject another existing projects.owner_user_id;
consume the application review ticket;
set projects.owner_user_id to the applicant's Testnet users.id;
create the project_owner_profiles row only if the profile is absent; reject conflicting existing profile ownership;
copy only the approved applicant profile/contact fields;
keep project_owner_profiles.verification_status='pending' unless a separate verification process has approved those profile details;
write application transition history and mark the application approved in one transaction.
There is no cross-database transaction spanning Mainnet and Testnet. The remote Mainnet revalidation must therefore be immediately before the Testnet transaction and its result must be short-lived and single-use.
Do not write owner_albukhr_user_id to Testnet. Do not write anything to Mainnet.
