10. Migration and rollout order
Recover/compare complete current migration and function source baseline; do not replay any migration.
Add forward-only Testnet migration for private provenance, application/history/ticket tables, indexes, constraints, RLS, grants and narrow RPCs.
Update mirror transaction to populate private provenance from the already-returned Mainnet source id; run a controlled registry sync and verify exact mappings for DAN-COS-001 and MAITAGOGO-2457.
Deploy the new Mainnet proof issuer with independent proof secret; do not replace ordinary Mainnet login issuer.
Deploy the Testnet application proof/owner endpoint and separate Admin endpoint.
Run API and SQL regression tests while UI is still hidden.
Add project-detail CTA/form and the separate Admin queue.
Test all failure cases and financial regression controls.
Enable the UI only after all server-side gates pass.
Rollback is feature disable / UI hide plus function rollback to the prior version where safe. Do not delete approved applications, provenance or audit history. Never reverse or rewrite applied migration history.
11. Critical risks closed by this design
Login assertions can no longer be mistaken for project-owner authorization.
Mainnet canonical Owner UUID never leaks into Testnet.
Browser cannot choose applicant identity, project type, approval state or reviewer identity.
A valid proof cannot be replayed or moved to another project or Testnet user.
A mirror with the same project code but a different source UUID is rejected.
Owner changes or project suspension on Mainnet are detected at approval time.
Legacy Core Owner Admin route and financial functions are not reused.
Core projects cannot apply, even if the UI is manipulated.
